---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import Evidence from '../components/Evidence.astro'
import Calculator from '../components/Calculator.astro'
import Problem from '../components/Problem.astro'
import Services from '../components/Services.astro'
import SampleCall from '../components/SampleCall.astro'
import Comparison from '../components/Comparison.astro'
import Process from '../components/Process.astro'
import Commercials from '../components/Commercials.astro'
import About from '../components/About.astro'
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro'
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro'
---

<Base>
  {/*
    Order is deliberate, and it is built around a reader who arrives from a
    cold email already half-suspicious. Each section answers the question the
    previous one creates.

      Hero        What is this, and what does it cost me in effort?
      Evidence    Says who? — cited third-party research, not our claims
      Calculator  Fine, but is it a problem for ME? — their own arithmetic
      Problem     Where exactly does it leak?
      Services    So what do you actually do about it?
      SampleCall  Does it sound like a robot? — the objection that kills this
      Comparison  Why not just do X instead?
      Process     How much of my time and what breaks?
      Commercials What am I agreeing to? — terms only once they believe it works
      About       Is there a real person behind this?
      FAQ         Everything left, including the awkward ones
      CTA         The one next step

    Two rules if you reorder. The calculator stays high, because it makes the
    visitor prove the problem to themselves before we ask them to believe
    anything about us. Commercial terms stay after the transcript, because
    nobody cares what it costs until they believe it works.
  */}
  <Hero />
  <Evidence />
  <Calculator />
  <Problem />
  <Services />
  <SampleCall />
  <Comparison />
  <Process />
  <Commercials />
  <About />
  <Faq />
  <Cta />
</Base>
